1. Purpose
This document records issues discovered during testing of the European Summer Travel Website.
Findings are separated from testing results so that the project maintains a clear distinction between:
Test
  ↓
Observation
  ↓
Analysis
  ↓
Finding
  ↓
Recommendation
2. Finding Categories
Findings may relate to:
•	Functionality
•	Accessibility
•	Security
•	Performance
•	Compatibility
•	Maintainability
3. Example Finding — Missing Alt Text
Finding ID: WEB-001
Severity: Low
Category: Accessibility
Title: Image missing alternative text
Evidence:
An image element does not contain meaningful alternative text.
Impact:
Users relying on screen readers may not receive information about the image.
Recommendation:
Add descriptive alt text.
Example:
<img
    src="santorini.jpg"
    alt="White buildings overlooking the sea in Santorini"
>
________________________________________
4. Example Finding — Broken Local Link
Finding ID: WEB-002
Severity: Medium
Category: Functionality
Title: Broken destination link
Evidence:
A navigation link points to a local HTML resource that cannot be found.
Impact:
Visitors may be unable to access the selected destination page.
Recommendation:
Verify the filename and update the link.
Example:
<a href="greece.html">
    Greece
</a>
________________________________________
5. Example Finding — HTTP External Resource
Finding ID: WEB-003
Severity: Medium
Category: Security
Title: External resource loaded over HTTP
Evidence:
A page references an external resource using:
http://
instead of:
https://
Impact:
Unencrypted external resources can be exposed to modification or observation during network transit.
Recommendation:
Use HTTPS resources whenever the provider supports them.
________________________________________
6. Example Finding — Missing Security Headers
Finding ID: WEB-004
Severity: Medium
Category: Security
Title: Security headers not configured
Evidence:
The deployed website does not return expected security-related HTTP response headers.
Potential Impact:
The absence of appropriate headers can reduce browser-side security protections.
Recommendation:
Configure appropriate response headers on the web server or hosting platform.
Examples include:
Content-Security-Policy
X-Content-Type-Options
Referrer-Policy
Strict-Transport-Security
This finding applies to the deployed website, not simply the local HTML files.
7. Example Finding — Inline JavaScript
Finding ID: WEB-005
Severity: Informational
Category: Maintainability / Security
Title: Inline JavaScript detected
Evidence:
JavaScript functionality is embedded directly inside the HTML document.
Impact:
Inline scripts can make strict Content Security Policy configuration more difficult.
Recommendation:
Move JavaScript into an external JavaScript file where practical.
Example:
js/
└── main.js
and:
<script src="js/main.js"></script>
